<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The two warnings this app accepts, and the reason for each. Everything else
  lint can see is fixed, so a new warning is the only one on the list.

  The legacy launcher tile is a full sheet of paper on purpose: it is the same
  paper as the adaptive icon's background, and Android 7.0 and 7.1, the only
  releases that read it, draw a legacy icon inside their own white circle or
  squircle, where a paper card reads as the app's page. The drawing is
  `tools/icons/forge.py`'s, and rounding the tile would change the app's face
  on the two releases that still read it (owner decision, this session).

  The themed layer is one silhouette of the book on its stand, traced at the
  size the shape is read at. Its path is long because the book's own curves
  are, and the launcher parses it once per icon set, never the app.
-->
<lint>
    <issue id="IconLauncherShape">
        <ignore path="src/main/res/mipmap-mdpi/ic_launcher.png" />
        <ignore path="src/main/res/mipmap-hdpi/ic_launcher.png" />
        <ignore path="src/main/res/mipmap-xhdpi/ic_launcher.png" />
        <ignore path="src/main/res/mipmap-xxhdpi/ic_launcher.png" />
        <ignore path="src/main/res/mipmap-xxxhdpi/ic_launcher.png" />
    </issue>
    <issue id="VectorPath">
        <ignore path="src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_monochrome.xml" />
    </issue>
    <!-- Lint asks for a fullBackupContent beside dataExtractionRules because
         that attribute only exists from Android 12 on. It is not needed:
         allowBackup="false" already refuses every backup and restore on
         Android 11 and below, which is the whole of what the legacy
         exclusions would say. The file that said it twice was deleted, and the
         privacy page is the one place the reader is told (owner decision,
         this session). -->
    <issue id="DataExtractionRules">
        <ignore path="src/main/AndroidManifest.xml" />
    </issue>
</lint>
